  "description": "XAFDOX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H96 La6 Mo4 N14 O66,4(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 11 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 10 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 9 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Mo2 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; La1A (La) has 11 O neighbors; Mo1A (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; La2A (La) has 10 O neighbors; Mo2A (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; La3A (La) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.024-5.261 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 151.00-170.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H128N14O70La6Mo4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
